>> I was wondering if it's possible to do so in a Unix envrionment?
[...]
> Download from the same site either in the incoming directory or from
> /pub/thomas/bones/unix

     That isn't going to work reliably.  Bones files contain binary
data, and since Unix runs on a wide variety of hardware and is built
with just as wide a variety of C compilers, the contents of those
files will not generally be compatible even when using the same set
of NetHack configuration options.  Things like byte order of multi-byte
integers, structure padding for optimum alignment, and layout of bit
fields will all pose problems.

     Also, ordinary Unix players will not be able to copy bones files
into their system's shared playground directory.



